  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1-preview.18\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.18 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.17\n- Fixed FCM registration failing with HTTP 401 UNAUTHENTICATED. The x-goog-firebase-installations-auth header now uses the official `FIS {token}` scheme (matching the Web JS SDK) instead of `FIS_v2 {token}`. The service worker's cold-start re-registration was updated to match.\n- Added a configurable default notification icon. The service worker now resolves relative notification icon/image/badge values to absolute URLs against the app origin, and the new MessagingBrowserOptions.DefaultNotificationIcon is provisioned to the worker as the fallback icon when the payload supplies none.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.16\n- Fixed RegisterAsync throwing ArgumentNullException when called without RegisterOptions. Registration with a null options now uses the configured MessagingBrowserOptions.VapidKey as documented (null = defaults), instead of crashing.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.15\n- Fixed ServiceWorkerPath and ServiceWorkerScope being ignored. The page JS module now accepts (path, scope), and the interop/adapter/lifecycle coordinator forward the configured values to navigator.serviceWorker.register. Consuming apps can now point registration at the package's shipped service worker (e.g. /_content/FireForNet.Firebase.Messaging.Browser/fireForNet-messaging-sw.js) without vendoring a copy into their own wwwroot.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.14\n- Initial browser Firebase Messaging integration: FID-based registration, foreground/notification event relay, permission management, config-free service worker, capability detection.\n- Uses IFirebaseInstallations directly for the FIS auth token and persistent FID.",
